pplicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATOH KATSUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATOH, KATSUMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATOH KATSUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATOH, KATSUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A press contact semiconductor device (1) having a ring-like gate terminal, not involving the technical problem that the gate current is not supplied uniformly to a semiconductor substrate (4) caused by the connection structure between the device (1) and an external gate driver (2). A ring-like gate terminal (10) is provided as a resistor having a resistivity of over 0.1 m OMEGA .cm. The voltage drop across the resistor is increased at a portion where the gate current is concentrated, and the gate current is distributed to other non-concentration portions. The press contact semiconductor device can be employed as a high power element in a power application apparatus.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif (1) semi-conducteur à contact à pression présentant une borne de grille du type anneau, qui permet de résoudre le problème technique que constitue un apport non uniforme de courant de grille à un substrat (4) de semi-conducteur en raison de la structure de connexion entre le dispositif (1) et un circuit d'attaque (2) de grille externe. Une borne (10) de grille du type anneau servant de résistance présente une résistivité supérieure à 0,1 m OMEGA .cm. La chute de tension dans la résistance est accrue à une partie qui concentre le courant de grille, et le courant de grille est distribué vers d'autres parties ne concentrant pas le courant. Le dispositif semi-conducteur à contact à pression peut être utilisé comme élément de grande puissance dans un appareil d'application de puissance.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>